#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# Precision and numerics

#% text
# Three kinds of numbers: exact (integers, rationals, `sqrt(2)`, `pi`), machine reals (about 16 digits) and arbitrary precision balls with a guaranteed error bound. `n` converts between them; the numerical functions take `working_precision:`.

#% section
# Exact, machine and arbitrary precision

#% cell
q = 1/3 + 2/7

#% cell
n(q)
#% output
#= 0.6190476190476191

#% cell
n(q, 40)
#% output
#= 0.61904761904761904761904761904761904761904762

#% cell
n(pi, 50)
#% output
#= 3.141592653589793238462643383279502884197169399375105821

#% cell
precision(1/3)
#% output
#= inf

#% cell
precision(1.5)
#% output
#= 15.954589770191003

#% text
# Mixing kinds gives the least exact one: a single machine real makes the result a machine real, so ask for digits at the start.

#% cell
n(pi, 30) + 1/2
#% output
#= 3.6415926535897932384626433832795029

#% cell
n(pi, 30) + 0.5
#% output
#= 3.641592653589793

#% cell
0.1 + 0.2
#% output
#= 0.30000000000000004

#% section
# Numerical functions with working_precision

#% cell
n_integrate(exp(-x^2), [x, 0, 1], working_precision: 30)
#% output
#= 0.74682413281242702539946743613185

#% cell
find_root(cos(x) == x, [x, 1], working_precision: 30)
#% output
#= [x -> 0.739085133215160641655312087674]

#% cell
n_sum(1/factorial(k), [k, 0, inf], working_precision: 30)
#% output
#= 2.7182818284590452353602874713526625

#% text
# `n_minimize` returns the minimum found and where; here it is the global one of this quartic, whose two valleys are near -1.3 and 1.1.

#% cell
n_minimize(x^4 - 3x^2 + x, [x, 1])
#% output
#= [-3.5139050389347886, [x -> -1.300839565941577]]

#% text
# `rationalize` returns exact values, `set_precision` changes a number's precision, `chop` drops tiny parts.

#% cell
rationalize(0.75)
#% output
#= 3/4

#% cell
set_precision(0.1, 30)
#% output
#= 0.100000000000000005551115123126

#% cell
chop(n(exp(pi*im)))
#% output
#= -1.0

#% section
# Common mistakes

#% item
# `n(x, 20)` of a result that cancelled is shorter than 20 digits; ask for more at the start.

#% cell
n(sqrt(2), 20)^2 - 2
#% output
#= ball(-2.0679515313825691872e-25, 4.08e-25)

#% item
# Machine reals round every operation: do exact work first.

#% cell
1.0e30 + 1 - 1.0e30
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
10^30 + 1 - 10^30
#% output
#= 1

#% item
# The imaginary unit is `im`.

#% cell
n(exp(1 + 2im))
#% output
#= -1.1312043837568135 + 2.4717266720048188im

#% section
# Related functions

#% text
# `n`, `precision`, `n_integrate`, `find_root`, `n_sum`, `n_minimize`, `rationalize`, `set_precision`
